::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
Describe g(x)=f(x)+3.
{
=A. Shift up 3#Correct. Adding outside changes outputs upward.
~B. Shift down 3#That would be f(x)-3.
~C. Shift left 3#Horizontal shifts happen inside the input.
~D. Shift right 3#That would involve f(x-3).
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
Describe g(x)=f(x-4).
{
~A. Shift left 4#Inside shifts use the opposite sign.
=B. Shift right 4#Correct. Subtracting inside the input shifts the graph right.
~C. Shift up 4#Vertical shifts occur outside.
~D. Reflect across x-axis#Reflection would use a negative outside.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
Describe g(x)=-f(x).
{
~A. Reflect across the y-axis#That would be f(-x).
~B. Shift down 1#A negative is not a vertical shift.
=C. Reflect across the x-axis#Correct. A negative outside changes output signs.
~D. Shift right 1#A negative outside is not horizontal.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
Describe g(x)=f(x+2)-5.
{
~A. Shift right 2 and down 5#Inside signs reverse.
~B. Shift left 2 and up 5#The outside -5 shifts down.
~C. Shift right 5 and down 2#This mixes the values.
=D. Shift left 2 and down 5#Correct. Adding inside shifts left; subtracting outside shifts down.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
Which rule shifts f left 6?
{
=A. g(x)=f(x+6)#Correct. Adding inside shifts left.
~B. g(x)=f(x-6)#This shifts right 6.
~C. g(x)=f(x)+6#This shifts up 6.
~D. g(x)=f(x)-6#This shifts down 6.
}

